#: b4142d10e89b44f9b0c6482de311b44f
msgid ""
"You will need two servos. One for the tilting action and one for the pan "
"action. Tilt is the moving of the antennas only and the pan could move the "
"whole AT or just the antennas depending on how you have yours designed. "
"Servos are actually complicated little devices. I'll try to be precise as "
"you can use the internet to find more details on servos if you wish. You "
"want a servo that can do at least 110 oz-in of torque for two patch "
"antennas, I'd recommend at least the `karbonite materials "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karbonite_gears>`__ to ensure it never strips"
" out, but you can get by on the nylon versions."
msgstr ""
"您需要两个舵机，一个用于俯仰动作，一个用于偏航动作。俯仰是仅移动天线，而偏航则根据您的设计可以移动整个天线追踪器或只移动天线。舵机实际上是相当复杂的小型设备。我尽量说得精确，如果您想了解更多关于舵机的细节，可以上网查找。对于两个贴片天线，您需要一个至少能提供"
" 110 oz-in 扭矩的舵机，我建议至少使用 `karbonite 材质 "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karbonite_gears>`__ 以确保永不打滑，但尼龙版本也可以凑合。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:120
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:121
#: 0d967ea12f3d44d2a4e8652400568a14 2334263494c640f08e457c17dfbda734
#: a3d4eeceeb664d059640027b1a9e4757 a98920ce02234629993101964a53b253
#: f27f2cd3ddaa49a3bcb4972218c8e88f
msgid ""
"For the tilt servo get a servo that does 90deg of rotation TOTAL. Different "
"manufacturers explain the total amount of rotation a servo can do in "
"different ways so you must really do your homework. 90deg rotation total is "
"a \"standard\" servo."
msgstr ""
"对于俯仰舵机，选择总旋转角度为 90 度的舵机。不同制造商描述舵机总旋转量的方式不同，因此您必须认真做功课。总旋转 90 度是「标准」舵机。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:125
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:126
#: 2b4334cd4e6746829e0811388417a9a2 31be7ef802db4e54a0d340cf3e058ba6
#: b23bc52ca79b4c8abaf1a3b02b958d7f b8f7db1d60c74f7d8345d17d0a2afa07
#: c4021fac04ad42a3bd5c9f21f1e2ff7f
msgid ""
"For the pan (this AT in particular, your requirements will vary) I'd "
"recommend at least 150+ oz-in of torque for two antennas and karbonite or "
"better, as in all metal gears. If you can get one, go digital (highly "
"recommend it) as the AT here is capable of small corrective actions and an "
"analogue servo will probably not be able to keep up like a digital servo "
"will. The reason for this overall beefiness is that when your panning range "
"is at the limit of travel your AT will rapidly spin itself around 360deg in "
"order to keep the antennas on target `(1:50 second mark as an example). "
"<https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=endscreen&v=_lxUd96-1tw&NR=1>`__ The "
"faster it does this the less time you are out of communication with your "
"aircraft. You can not avoid this behavior if you use the APM Mission Planner"
" as the behavior is embedded in the software. Building an AT that does not "
"care about the pan range is very expensive to do as it starts to involve "
"what are known as slip rings. The military uses them and they are very nice,"
" but very expensive due to the quality of slip ring involved. If you can do "
"this then you avoid cable tangling issues and possibly servo range selection"
" gets easier. For this build the pan action you want is a servo that can do "
"360deg of rotation. You really don't need more than that."
msgstr ""
"对于偏航（针对此特定天线追踪器，您的需求可能不同），我建议两个天线至少使用 150+ oz-in 的扭矩，并使用 karbonite "
"或更好的全金属齿轮。如果可能，选择数字舵机（强烈推荐），因为这里的天线追踪器能够进行小幅修正动作，模拟舵机可能跟不上数字舵机的响应速度。需要如此强力规格的原因是，当您的偏航范围达到行程极限时，天线追踪器会迅速自转"
" 360 度以保持天线对准目标 `（视频 1:50 时间点示例）。 "
"<https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=endscreen&v=_lxUd96-1tw&NR=1>`__ "
"转速越快，您与飞行器失联的时间越短。如果使用 APM Mission "
"Planner，则无法避免此行为，因为该行为已嵌入软件中。构建不受偏航范围限制的天线追踪器非常昂贵，需要使用所谓的滑环。军方使用滑环，质量非常好，但价格非常高昂。如果能实现这一点，您就可以避免电缆缠绕问题，舵机行程选择也可能更容易。对于本构建，偏航动作需要一个能旋转"
" 360 度的舵机，不需要更多。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:147
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:148
#: 7699d03ee4344cb4be2a2d8a4e4d559e 7785d32e0d5a45508cb9e2ee1f288398
#: 950a718f0377431ca51fcb94ec235c6c c5f46b99f39d4afdaf4b44e5ff7dc0b7
#: dffbf32173fc4870b98a4f7e512234c8
msgid "Servo Control"
msgstr "舵机控制"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:149
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:150
#: 22c2d1a4163144d0b7180deb38c34ccb 2e3c4d9e7cc44560b148973db0ae7b25
#: 4a1d3ce7913345618e6c3deb9aa9d3e8 d303449d829e4a819c99db4ee9a0c3f5
#: d4a1d123dfc2459ba42848f8bc862abe
msgid ""
"You will need something to take the information from your computer (again "
"this build used the APM Mission Planner to drive the AT) and turn those into"
" a signal (numbers really) that your servo can use. The APM MP has two "
"options currently, one for `Maestro <https://www.pololu.com/product/1350>`__"
" and one for `ArduPilot <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/retired/8785>`__."
" The Maestro link is to a SERVO CONTROLLER card and the ArduPilot is both a "
"servo controller and a stripped down autopilot (it is actually the original "
"APM being used as a servo controller card). To be more clear, in some "
"articles the ArduPilot is referred to as the ArduTracker. The Maestro can "
"run up to 6 servos with the input provided by the micro USB cable but you "
"will only use 2 of them plus the power pins. The ArduPilot version uses one "
"of the early versions of the APM called ArduPilot. It is stripped down and "
"cheap, you might have one from years ago, I don't know much about it, but "
"`this is a build <https://code.google.com/archive/p/happykillmore-"
"gcs/wikis/Tracking.wiki>`__ that HappyKilmore's GCS uses and `they "
"<https://www.diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/antenna-tracking-"
"in?xg_source=activity>`__ did a write up on both of them. I used it a lot "
"and you can't go wrong reading it yourself either! No matter which "
"controller type you use to drive your servos you WILL need to download and "
"install the firmware for them. Maestro came preloaded and it looks like you "
"need to find the firmware for the ArduPilot card from their website or this "
"website's software library."
msgstr ""
"您需要某种东西来从计算机（同样，本构建使用 APM Mission Planner "
"来驱动天线追踪器）获取信息，并将其转换为舵机可以使用的信号（实际上是数字）。APM Mission Planner 目前有两个选项，一个用于 "
"`Maestro <https://www.pololu.com/product/1350>`__，一个用于 `ArduPilot "
"<https://www.sparkfun.com/products/retired/8785>`__。Maestro "
"链接是舵机控制卡，ArduPilot 既是舵机控制器也是精简版飞控（实际上是用作舵机控制卡的原始 APM）。更明确地说，在某些文章中，ArduPilot"
" 被称为 ArduTracker。Maestro 可通过 Micro USB 电缆提供的输入驱动最多 6 个舵机，但您只需使用其中 2 "
"个加上电源引脚。ArduPilot 版本使用早期版本的 APM，即 ArduPilot，它是精简版且价格低廉，您可能有几年前的旧货，我对它了解不多，但 "
"`这是一个构建案例 <https://code.google.com/archive/p/happykillmore-"
"gcs/wikis/Tracking.wiki>`__，是 HappyKilmore 的 GCS 使用的，`他们 "
"<https://www.diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/antenna-tracking-"
"in?xg_source=activity>`__ "
"对两者都做了介绍。我经常使用它，您自己阅读也不会有什么损失！无论您使用哪种控制器类型来驱动舵机，都需要下载并安装对应固件。Maestro "
"预装了固件，ArduPilot 卡的固件需要从其官网或本站软件库中查找。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:173
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:174
#: 75c05a0ae9214cf2aefa3692c0b7e401 a6bd0a609f8a4046afc4d77be68e1823
#: c9c44e8c1ed14fa69a9c30c355afbd9b e1c6020f2c1a47409b9144d5040037c0
#: eb5343fa56c74f3eaeb50e5d36440f0a
msgid ""
"Getting the right numbers for your servo controller is vital, `use this as a"
" guide <http://vps.oborne.me/gcs/Tracker.html>`__. Basically you will find "
"two numbers that bookend the total rotation your servo will do which could "
"be less than what it can do but not more, then you will find the center of "
"those bookends and then you will tell Maestro the \"8-bit\" range that it "
"should use as commands to send to the servos. It's way critical to get these"
" right, I lost hair doing it."
msgstr ""
"获取正确的舵机控制器参数至关重要，`请以此为参考 "
"<http://vps.oborne.me/gcs/Tracker.html>`__。基本上，您需要找到两个数值作为舵机总旋转的书签（可以小于舵机实际能做到的，但不能超过），然后找到这两个书签的中点，再告诉"
" Maestro 发送给舵机的命令应使用的「8 位」范围。这非常关键，务必搞对，我为此费了不少心思。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:183
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:184
#: 1bd7defbf2ba45fcb447b8b79092379a 6d5e52134ac1474ba5bea760899d5d99
#: 95ce4001d4ac4b3baef6979d90e8e376 af911bf05f154d6ca275b279835174de
#: d8d86c5d38814acdb477246db9d97b89
msgid ""
"Ok, servos run off of 4.8, 6 or sometimes 7.2V or more. Most of them default"
" to the RC standby voltage of \"5V\". This one is running off of 6V. This "
"battery puts out 12.5V when charged fully. If you do not find a way to step "
"down the voltage from your battery to the CORRECT usable voltage for your "
"servo you will fry your servo. Your servo motor might smoke or the little "
"tiny tiny circuit board in it might smoke, either way the reliability of it "
"is gone and you should get a NEW SERVO. If you don't and it fails in flight,"
" you could lose connection because your AT can not point properly! A BEC "
"(Battery Eliminating Circuit) is what you are looking for here. This project"
" used `this one <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-3a-ubec-w-noise-"
"reduction.html?___store=en_us>`__. If you do your homework, you can look up "
"the idle and full load current consumption of your chosen servos and pick a "
"BEC that will handle that load. If you fail to get a BEC that can handle the"
" spontaneous most highest ever load your servo could possibly generate then "
"it will fry and your power to point your AT will be gone, bye bye aircraft."
msgstr ""
"舵机使用 4.8V、6V 或有时 7.2V 及以上的电压运行。大多数默认使用 RC 待机电压「5V」。这个使用 6V 运行。这块电池充满时输出 "
"12.5V。如果您不找方法将电池电压降到舵机正确可用的电压，您将烧毁舵机。舵机电机可能会冒烟，或其内部那块小小的电路板可能会冒烟，无论哪种情况，其可靠性都将丧失，您应该换一个新舵机。如果不这样做，它在飞行中失效，您的天线追踪器将无法正常指向，您的飞行器可能因此失联！BEC（电池消除电路）正是您需要的。本项目使用了"
" `这款 <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-3a-ubec-w-noise-"
"reduction.html?___store=en_us>`__。如果您做好功课，查找所选舵机的空载和满载电流消耗，就可以选择能承受该负载的 "
"BEC。如果选用的 BEC 无法承受舵机可能产生的最大瞬时负载，它将烧毁，您为天线追踪器供电的能力也将丧失，飞行器再见。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:200
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:201
#: 015ba448843242219534af9dcd34d5f6 28e0c82440d24761901d7010ab44fc03
#: 3667833689af4209a2067f52da3e1e4e 38ac021997a447a1b288e5e55d6cd9b2
#: a7421441519d4e838a6b8915d85b779d
msgid "Battery low-voltage warning device"
msgstr "电池低电压报警装置"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:202
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:203
#: 14094c3c3f764adb8081cd8674899833 2be21c568bee4a85bfefd91a011825c9
#: d36841607f294bcfb2e754fea64f1dd3 d753d1f1c36d4a8dad9ea2e174142510
#: fd0e871257414badb91e09028bcde4f8
msgid ""
"You don't have to use this, but I would. It is cheap and could save not only"
" your battery but it will tell you when your AT is about to quit. It is "
"about as loud as a smoke detector going off! Buy a few of these and use "
"them, don't be cheap like that, seriously."
msgstr ""
"您不必使用这个，但我会用。它价格低廉，不仅能保护您的电池，还会告诉您天线追踪器何时快要停止工作。它的声音大约和烟雾报警器一样响！多买几个使用，别舍不得那点钱，说真的。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:208
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:209
#: 619e505a0a804ab897c75c1419a7e398 8b151b2ecbf546e997afe6e4525e8a90
#: 961f2af879704b149b5c1aa11f69d0b7 cc7f4ba8fbcf4dcfbc2a7e42286d780d
#: f37395b95d09490c95fdf67795c3b638
msgid "Video Rx and Tx"
msgstr "视频接收机和发射机"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:210
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:211
#: 0087033888d6455b9e39b6cd4000e605 26937a61c6074aa7b9ed3455efe8a8e7
#: 91c13b38098f41139a410b5fd212adaf 96bbd9f1f81c476f86f2551c4fa3b326
#: e09b12c951f84784b2d2f98938da418e
msgid ""
"Rx and Tx is shorthand for Receiver and Transmitter respectively. It is not "
"in the scope of the AT build guide here to tell you about these but instead "
"it is just to tell you that whichever system you use make sure it can fit to"
" your AT. Your AT is going to get crowded and messy and therefore it can "
"bind on the smallest of things. Binding is bad, ok?"
msgstr ""
"Rx 和 Tx "
"分别是接收机和发射机的缩写。本天线追踪器构建指南不涉及这些的详细说明，只是提醒您，无论使用哪种系统，确保它能安装到您的天线追踪器上。您的天线追踪器会变得拥挤而杂乱，因此可能被最小的东西卡住。卡住是不好的，明白了吗？"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:217
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:218
#: 3b14567a41494d66828a5abcb67aef94 65edbc010cc8412eb6f2f1b13c8c49dc
#: 707f5858e4cd4f938fb9c9dd18cfda36 a8368c7393a0423188c0274aede6b6c0
#: d549611c8ec144c593cec3a7495e8b80
msgid "Tripod"
msgstr "三脚架"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:219
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:220
#: 0f7dd5a3ecfe4e39a7069bfeef5114a0 175af40a157c41aaaade459cd9801cd5
#: 30424d904d674449a9b95e10f13047ae 6338e0dfed23433e8a5b1a4a5bc664f4
#: ffb9e03821c647ca8267553d35d8d2e4
msgid ""
"You could come up with another thing to use, but that would be tantamount to"
" reinventing the wheel. The higher your AT is the further it can spread its "
"signal. Try to get one that does not have a lot of protrusions like this one"
" has. They will eventually entangle your wires. Pay attention to which type "
"of connector the tripod uses so you can design your AT to link to it. Get "
"one that is sturdy as a nice bit of wind could knock it over and your "
"aircraft goes link dead. Your AT should weigh around 7 lbs max, probably "
"less depending on what you use."
msgstr ""
"您可以想出其他替代方案，但那无异于重新发明轮子。天线追踪器安装得越高，信号传播距离越远。尽量选择没有太多突起的三脚架，否则会缠绕您的电线。注意三脚架使用的连接器类型，以便您可以设计天线追踪器与之适配。选择坚固的三脚架，一阵大风可能将其吹倒，您的飞行器就会失联。您的天线追踪器重量应不超过约"
" 7 磅，具体取决于您使用的材料，可能更轻。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:229
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:230
#: 20cdadc15c1e45baaef63ddf6c16f164 3f882524219843d185025328b3dac4a4
#: 444392b05ff944ac98a07b791e21c168 a12c80ce04e4428e9cf92b1e2d97758c
#: ae77bd65e24b4554833a1ddfbb5fdadf
msgid "Picture gallery"
msgstr "图片集"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:253
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:254
#: 0edf51a61a684ef08ee676295392950f 58d2b1c2de284a54acc3367847a228fe
#: 6892d4a53c084caeb27e7fc5eff87b3c cadb4b27b6404591837a2653a0d215e2
#: eccc5f5546da49158371bbea45a6026d
msgid "Connecting the parts"
msgstr "连接各部件"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:255
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:256
#: 1c12e9a28b0a4352b08b74be30a1f7cb 48c8cdfef11e4c09aaf8ba3f90600f0b
#: 9b236c46c2b5492f80518b3d78c9c32e a088c9245f204c0ab2e95bfdd4e08cfd
#: acb90c8a77844f6e8163ae5ae52b8cf6
msgid "**VELCRO AND ZIP-TIES, you can use them to a very large degree here!**"
msgstr "**魔术贴和扎带，在这里可以大量使用！**"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:257
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:258
#: 28ef1e2a7122414c97fb95d299f286f5 9d45f805ea8a4f11a79421ee3240ebea
#: b34582ab3fcc47bf84a97b9c2f47f8d1 b4bd332b037649ac820ed857f1dc1286
#: f24a23a55e334b50874879a5b0f7a67b
msgid ""
"1) Connect your servo controller board to your laptop, micro USB to USB for "
"Maestro."
msgstr "1) 将舵机控制板连接到笔记本电脑，Maestro 使用 Micro USB 转 USB。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:260
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:261
#: 1ba04103bfb8478c94b9ef9d4610928e 70763a904490454ca0d4ad9a1b3697a2
#: 78cb69f8cc924cf08ad73891828aaa5e 8979d7c09e6f460084f365b62e7e2e6c
#: fd4946207e0f445b8afd915b1707a45d
msgid ""
"2) Servos connect to the servo controller board. For Maestro it will be "
"servo 0 pin set for pan and servo 1 pin set for tilt."
msgstr "2) 舵机连接到舵机控制板。对于 Maestro，将 servo 0 引脚设为水平旋转，将 servo 1 引脚设为俯仰倾斜。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:263
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:264
#: 249694f1e31b4d30aea2df7fb01f2d7b 2c39a062a80345bdbae1298bc197c40c
#: 3df5ee7d02ee476caf6da934b41dad90 41678aa4021d467a9009ce9608504821
#: f0a5d4dc79314eb79723ba5b27685a4a
msgid ""
"3) Connect your battery to your BEC which is set at 5V or 6V or whatever "
"your servos can handle (max it out). Connect the BEC to the servo controller"
" board. For Maestro the pin set on the outermost is for the BATTERY power "
"that will drive your servos (the USB cable powers the board). DON'T REVERSE "
"THE POLARITY, buy new stuff if you did."
msgstr ""
"3) 将电池连接到设置为 5V 或 6V（或舵机所能承受的最大电压）的 BEC。将 BEC 连接到舵机控制板。对于 "
"Maestro，最外侧的引脚用于连接驱动舵机的电池电源（USB 线为控制板供电）。切勿接反极性，否则请更换新配件。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:269
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:270
#: 1e306ed128c848e8a07dcec042447392 499638fe96a64152a270ababfae3b3f7
#: 6975fb963ff04d2292952e48580b9519 897d91c1aae7492f9690c73315eb9979
#: dac641ace69843fb82c77e16da693518
msgid ""
"4) Connect your battery (assuming Li-Po here) to the Low Voltage detection "
"device, pay attention to it."
msgstr "4) 将电池（此处假设为锂聚合物电池）连接到低电压检测设备，注意观察其状态。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:272
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:273
#: 26bf0cefea984b5ab4182caa0255f7c1 4135913ffb0741078743b1123a4fb972
#: 9cb5a9e02b1845c7addbf64391d9c52c e784e0f820fd47a48b26b0bf7ce69eea
#: f809689774994cd0ab9b4ee8099ab650
msgid ""
"5) Connect your antennas to your SiK Radio (NEVER TURN ON RADIOS WITHOUT "
"ANTENNA ATTACHED, buy new stuff if you did). Connect antenna to the Video "
"Rx."
msgstr "5) 将天线连接到 SiK 数传（切勿在未连接天线的情况下开启数传，否则请更换新配件）。将天线连接到图传接收机。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:276
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:277
#: 1e3309fbd9814be09cefdcdfa58d4f18 1f897b49eda04925abec81f7e43ef539
#: 33c97136ca104eab91456fce35af9fa0 4a5625e04bb84eb08410c460259f2c0b
#: b5afe45e801b4cdd875ad7142f15d937
msgid ""
"6) You will need to splice off the power from the 12V side of the battery "
"connection to feed 12V of power to your Video Rx, get some solder and a wet "
"sponge, do a good job on the connection. Connect the power to your Video Rx."
msgstr "6) 你需要从电池连接的 12V 端分出电源，为图传接收机提供 12V 电压，准备好焊锡和湿海绵，务必做好连接。将电源连接到图传接收机。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:281
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:282
#: 1794cb35ca0845928b232493ae21b84e 20def485dcd84658b47a18b79f0a2b9f
#: b29444192c7744b597a8fa898093430a b610d5b29347405b814c35b03c7101e8
#: f6137e77c4d64614af9510e110b8704a
msgid ""
"7) Connect your 3DR 900Mhz radio to the laptop (after you have antenna "
"connected)."
msgstr "7) 将 3DR 900MHz 数传连接到笔记本电脑（请先确保天线已连接）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:284
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:285
#: 037382939c914c0993a77163b5ef70cb a0275263f6f442538978a0b37cb5c09f
#: bd6cd15587b34ec9a01d0dd457ecd7ce ceac4dfe7749428497bde0f923a103ad
#: f257a53e81c346b2908eaa0c41e3da72
msgid ""
"8) Use a bunch of zip-ties to secure and bundle all the wires. This is "
"important. If you do a bad job here your AT will bind while its tracking and"
" down goes aircraft."
msgstr "8) 使用扎带固定并捆绑所有导线，这非常重要。如果处理不好，天线追踪器在追踪时可能会被卡住，导致飞机坠毁。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:288
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:289
#: 2ead168e11b7458387f1e43cd76a5a61 52bc63fc1b764a9692618d180a9c2b00
#: 822d2646912f4c8dbe074f621d17c592 8350f2c1a42347889ac5a0ae3265f632
#: f426125b92e4404da8637dd4fe672719
msgid "add VELCRO AND ZIP-TIES to hold everything together"
msgstr "使用魔术贴和扎带将所有部件固定在一起"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:290
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:291
#: 31329f268f554f05a5e2f641e31e3258 66ad1c01e767437d89bf2c7b2d7965ec
#: e43ee5cac57348f8aa11bba5e9646f0c f0e1ca530ff041bba7171259fb5b322a
#: fbf3a855218e4af79c02fbbc3c5d7574
msgid ""
"10) Remember to set your end points manually in the Mission Planner for the "
"channels you will use to control pan and tilt, use a PWM value like 1100µs "
"and 1900µs with a midpoint of 1500µs to start. Some 180 degree servo's can "
"take 600-2400µs but you can damage some servo's so start conservatively."
msgstr ""
"10) 记得在 Mission Planner 中手动设置用于控制水平旋转和俯仰倾斜通道的端点，初始可使用 1100µs 和 1900µs 的 PWM "
"值，中点为 1500µs。部分 180 度舵机可接受 600-2400µs，但某些舵机可能因此损坏，请从保守值开始设置。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:297
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:298
#: 3e7b2f4156e749559f0739c100e1c1d8 47a87f7968664e8b95c6dcac0cbb9ac8
#: 91ba45eb43e5422b9062d0ce79a053d3 d913cd5fdb294a8c8c09a1ed65cc1b39
#: f4ecd766f062457481102500c63262f8
msgid "Basic use"
msgstr "基本使用"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:299
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:300
#: 345afe1d6ee74f769d68f62884b90c84 6e46799c17cf46e8a84e64c824d7b1d6
#: 7b0b811cb7f24c09bb09b84f91e90ee5 a2bb6e23133c4db0a14c8346785954aa
#: aa86777c469245f0ada3bcc29c1ba04a
msgid ""
"1) When you get to the airfield you point your AT north, get as close as you"
" can with your eyeball."
msgstr "1) 到达飞行场地后，用肉眼尽量将天线追踪器朝向正北方。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:302
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:303
#: 608a6491aa8c414a9763c5f49832679e 723f7371d3744b4ba8ed3e663b09ff26
#: dc8fbdc9f614431dab5c7c1dff5a8975 dfb6aa3dde774f41948dc099fed0e441
#: ec3e940b349846c09f17ad5aef0dbaf6
msgid ""
"2) Normal acceptable calibration for an AT is that you should be within "
"10deg of North when you point it."
msgstr "2) 天线追踪器的正常可接受校准误差是朝向偏差在 10 度以内。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:305
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:306
#: 2082605eded64a1cb27bcbeec6b27a29 8aa7a01ab9094206a04e442fe94e12eb
#: a483f815e1314f79ad038d78f76c7f58 f34426b1ca9142f59d5143606b4e3e55
#: fdca102cfbf642eabdd1386f58021045
msgid ""
"3) This particular body is able to be lifted, which separates the gear of "
"the servo from the smaller gear of the body. This allows it to be oriented "
"very easily. If you don't have that feature, just pick the thing up after it"
" finishes booting (and therefore is pointing at the default PWM number YOU "
"ASSIGNED when programming the servo controller)."
msgstr ""
"3) "
"此机体可以被抬起，从而将舵机齿轮与机体上的小齿轮分离，使方向调整非常方便。如果没有这个功能，只需在完成启动后（此时已按照你在编程舵机控制器时指定的默认 "
"PWM 值朝向预设方向）拿起设备重新放置即可。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:311
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:312
#: 353db2b518a14ff8ad7373c0d8d7294f 7ff32598a834426ca324363c511b2dbc
#: 8f9c9ccad62b4f2bae8fb39ed825d4ea dc3c4612dba94d199bdc1427141c96be
#: e190767870a4401aac827d896b433d5b
msgid ""
"4) You want the tilt to default to the middle of the tilting servo's travel "
"range, so for a 90deg servo, make it default to 45deg. When you actually USE"
" the antenna for the first time pay attention to the behavior of the tilting"
" and manually adjust it via the sliding bars in Mission Planner. If you're "
"confident about where it should be you can manually tweak the servo horn. "
"Either method will work but if you use the slider bar you will not "
"overstress the servo when it tries to go PAST it naturally allowed traveling"
" range."
msgstr ""
"4) 俯仰倾斜应默认设置在舵机行程范围的中间位置，例如对于 90 度舵机，应默认设为 45 度。第一次实际使用天线时，注意观察俯仰倾斜的动作，并通过 "
"Mission Planner "
"中的滑动条手动调整。如果对位置很有把握，也可以手动微调舵机摇臂。两种方法均可，但使用滑动条不会在舵机试图超出其允许行程时造成损伤。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:323
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:324
#: 004782dc5f634e76b24998f5577a10c4 2f059a1cbc2e4175814a958f917e6ef2
#: 3bb22f8de1aa4af985aaf56efb56fc95 91a2a0523d924b669151aa0cb8548903
#: ab3e4293b8de497cac5273a0875877d9
msgid ""
"While in flight you can use the slider bars to fine tune the direction the "
"antenna tracker is pointing."
msgstr "飞行过程中，可以使用滑动条微调天线追踪器的指向方向。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:326
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:327
#: 196727f9444c4f35897916eb2f50fee2 739a45c1d94e4d0cbb5c2eec0ac4a1c6
#: a47c02e7afa34531ad0704f53c30da74 baa9776bfaa64e3893d59063e5905da0
#: f61930eaf76a40fea85005f8454c706d
msgid ""
"5) If the servos are going in the wrong direction. Try clicking the Rev "
"checkbox to reverse travel direction. You may need to check off Rev before "
"connecting to the servo controller."
msgstr "5) 如果舵机方向不对，尝试勾选 Rev 复选框以反转行进方向。可能需要在连接舵机控制器之前先勾选 Rev。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:334
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:335
#: 12a8cf7870d046de8c019bff5790ee41 1fb88423b41f4ec68297653da39db330
#: 3b5afce086ce4fdaaeaa2e7e9b8ffca1 5723dd54dd7043b0b0b541362a3e7162
#: c25477715673425193eabbea9bf7ecc4
msgid "Advanced use"
msgstr "高级使用"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:338
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:339
#: 0d46f0764bcc4851869319476c7b90cc 41fea609791747e4b467291789e1e06f
#: a617fd328bbd49f1a28503bc089f1f9a b147a75320644e26bae684743ed22246
#: fc25f54c610e46e3a60554dcdf4a26a8
msgid ""
"This section is an excerpt from a post by Scott Fuller. The original post is"
" here: `The expensive but attention grabbing Antenna Tracker "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/the-expensive-but-attention-grabbing-"
"antenna-tracker>`__)"
msgstr ""
"本节摘录自 Scott Fuller 的文章。原文链接：`昂贵但引人注目的天线追踪器 "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/the-expensive-but-attention-grabbing-"
"antenna-tracker>`__)"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:341
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:342
#: 0b8f74cf73944425a963ed891e7fd402 0dded0a0794040cab2de62e47d82a3c8
#: 3994453841f944538cc95f09a9ff09fa 8e0b11d7f7c2453a885b3cca3148743b
#: eed643425480470ba0c6cdfa6f842189
msgid ""
"Usually the first thing I do is power up everything and get a solid GPS lock"
" on the APM. After that I'll set my plane in front of the antenna tracker "
"and zoom in REALLY tightly in Mission Planner under the Flight Planner "
"window. I'll then right click and say Tracker Home -> Set here."
msgstr ""
"通常我做的第一件事是给所有设备上电，并等待 APM 获得稳定的 GPS 定位。之后，我将飞机放在天线追踪器前面，在 Mission Planner "
"的飞行规划窗口中非常紧密地放大地图，右键单击并选择 Tracker Home -> Set here。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:349
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:350
#: 1ce5b8834bd44c60837107199e76d08c 9710f605b5934198b3cffb9b0ff073b8
#: 9a511809ee9a4bb4a1bd4bc74ec01080 be0b99d5a31a4c69a5300093117e60c4
#: e1142635fa4244f1865025a3b2cc1691
msgid ""
"*Then I'll drag the antenna tracker pin right on top of home and drop it. "
"That should get me pretty close to where my antenna tracker is placed.*"
msgstr "*然后我将天线追踪器图标直接拖放到 Home 点上。这样就能很接近天线追踪器的实际位置。*"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:356
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:357
#: 152280f16ec84c578b44df8c13022332 414c61d1014043c794cab704d7a38563
#: 9dba872a2ec84563b46fa0f0d92316ba aa97132c82f446b4bee142598a796bfc
#: c8e9276d800f4a30abd822e3c63027f3
msgid ""
"*After that I'll flip over to the Initial Setup tab under Antenna Tracker "
"and pull down the COM port for the Pololu servo controller and go with 9600 "
"baud. When that's set I hit connect. At that point the tracker should go "
"into motion.*"
msgstr ""
"*之后切换到天线追踪器下的初始设置选项卡，在下拉菜单中选择 Pololu 舵机控制器的 COM 口，波特率设为 "
"9600。设置完成后点击连接，此时追踪器应开始运动。*"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:364
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:365
#: 451057bce19a453fae391a60f3515aa0 8f00a924b3df4c3097ca5ac755940123
#: 99591e55c1134af1addcd981ba281ecc be01a14b3b0643b7919963c95af7965a
#: c309af60a15f4cf7a3640ab21881fd5d
msgid ""
"*You should be able to move the plane a few meters in front of the antenna "
"tracker should move with it. If you need to reverse the direction it's "
"pretty self explanatory. The sliders allow you to trim where the antenna "
"needs to be facing. When you start up the system will think you're facing "
"north. If you're facing East or West you have to aim accordingly.*"
msgstr ""
"*你应该能够将飞机移动几米，天线追踪器也会随之运动。如果需要反转方向，操作相当直观。滑动条用于微调天线的朝向。系统启动时会认为你朝向正北方。如果你朝向东方或西方，需要相应调整。*"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:371
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:372
#: 5fd5c6c844784fe6a7599a59d23a1f34 6e194853248b479ab6abd03ab01d651d
#: a2628c00af404648ba3ab3badf9ca3ca c2e84268d43e4df1b3c402e3304d2f80
#: db9489fe65504f51a372b109c38f9320
msgid ""
"*You can use Pololu Maestro Control Center to figure out your PWM settings "
"and how far your servos an travel. Usually the PWM setting is (Large Number "
"- Small Number) = PWM. In my case 2000 - 960 = 1040 for pan and 1904 - 1456 "
"= 448 for my tilt. That'll give me a 45 degree angle for tilt and 360 for "
"pan. You can get these numbers on the status tab in Maestro CC. Be careful "
"NOT to go beyond the recommended travel! On the Servo City gear boxes you'll"
" hear the POT start to click and the servo will just spin. At that point you"
" get to play the servo centering game.*"
msgstr ""
"*你可以使用 Pololu Maestro Control Center 确定 PWM 设置及舵机的行程范围。通常 PWM 设置为（大数 - 小数）= "
"PWM。我的例子中，水平旋转为 2000 - 960 = 1040，俯仰倾斜为 1904 - 1456 = 448。这给了我 45 度的俯仰角和 360"
" 度的旋转范围。这些数值可以在 Maestro CC 的状态选项卡中获得。注意不要超出推荐行程！在 Servo City "
"齿轮箱上，你会听到电位器开始卡嗒声，舵机会一直旋转。到那时你就需要重新进行舵机居中操作了。*"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:383
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:384
#: 1745e691790a471bba333e1262877417 270b24cd700848848bd3b5bc2c0fa5f9
#: 50f446336335441399a19f8718fd70fc abb5e8fda52249cd9e0e3869c88c72ea
#: d7290aaa2de745c88b11b6ebcdf5c880
msgid ""
"*One thing to note with the Pololu board is you may have to set it into USB "
"Dual Port under Serial Settings. This allows you to connect to the COM "
"port.*"
msgstr "*需要注意的是，Pololu 控制板可能需要在串口设置中设置为 USB 双端口模式，这样才能连接到 COM 口。*"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:388
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:389
#: 0999c94bdfb54158b97545f6ded6b9df 1f711d0c33f64ab2bc7c2a677e3510ae
#: 70fd913b8ac340fb90ff22cb7be66aad bf296f4ad40a46aca9abd1c1f6020bd7
#: ddf5c1ba24c14959befb8ff6875829dc
msgid "Miscellaneous notes"
msgstr "其他注意事项"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:390
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:391
#: 15a3fa7a90454abda99bc44dcec3cfb6 16ee70ef6f234f62bcd92123fda61de8
#: 65e33600bf8c465883ca2dd034abe256 87fcd6db52904aa3b731b0d1fc6661dc
#: be955ebd0b3f494f986b49620dd1ffeb
msgid ""
"I have included pictures from all angles of my AT (version 2). A few "
"pointers here. Build your AT as light as you can. Get as beefy of servos as "
"you can afford and fit. You can make a wireless version of this AT if you "
"have telemetry radios like the :ref:`3DR or the Xbee <common-telemetry-"
"landingpage>` kits. I don't know how to do that but it is not going to be "
"anymore complicated than what I have shown here, just more expensive."
msgstr ""
"我已从各角度拍摄了我的天线追踪器（第 2 版）的照片。一些要点：尽量把天线追踪器做得轻巧。在能力范围内尽量选用扭力强的舵机。如果你有 :ref:`3DR"
" 或 Xbee <common-telemetry-landingpage>` "
"等数传套件，可以制作无线版天线追踪器。我不知道具体如何实现，但应该不会比我展示的更复杂，只是成本更高。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:397
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:398
#: 0b52906681e04d8e84a6e04823217f5a 47e226e444964b2eb2ab593ea5233e5b
#: 50f1209896af4c7387b3758b43bb35ae 679e69f1315640d885620472d30294c2
#: ffa76d6a7e074efb924973c156be9730
msgid ""
"Testing is done in two ways, first you setup your AT outside and point it "
"north before you fire it up. Then walk around the AT with your plane with "
"everything linked up as if it was in flight. You need to get at LEAST 60 "
"feet away, try 100ft to make sure. Another way is to load a previously "
"recorded flight from the APM2 logs, set your home position and watch your AT"
" go at it as if it was there."
msgstr ""
"测试有两种方式：一是在户外将天线追踪器朝向正北后上电，然后携带飞机绕追踪器行走，一切连接如同在飞行中。需要至少走到 60 英尺以外，建议走到 100 "
"英尺以确保效果。另一种方式是加载 APM2 日志中之前录制的飞行记录，设置 Home 点，观察追踪器的追踪效果。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-gps-based-antenna-tracking.rst:404
